{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Israel dwelt in Shittim, etc.</b> One needs to know what need there is for the statement of this verse, and our Sages of blessed memory (Midrash Rabbah, Tanchuma) raised this issue and said that it comes to inform you that this was a cause for harlotry, etc., because the place by its nature arouses the nature of bestial desire. And it appears to explain that Scripture testifies to the cause of the harlotry, which was that the people went out to stroll outside the camp of Israel, and there the daughters of Moab were to be found; and that is its saying <b>and Israel dwelt in Shittim</b> — meaning, in the place where they would stroll outside their camp; and Shittim is an expression of strolling, in the manner of its saying (Numbers 11:8) ״שָׁטוּ הָעָם״, and Rashi there explained, and this is his language: שַׁיִט is nothing but an expression of strolling. And this is the cause of ״the people began to commit harlotry.״" "<b>The people began to commit harlotry with the daughters of Moab.</b> Its saying <b>וַיָּחֶל</b> is an expression of profanation — they became profaned through harlotry; meaning, because they went astray after foreign gods. And it says <b>with the daughters</b> etc., meaning, in the manner of our Sages of blessed memory (Midrash Rabbah and Tanchuma there) who said that they [the daughters of Moab] would demand of them [the Israelites] to transgress and would say to them, bow down to this, etc., and they would bow down to that which the daughters of Moab told them — and that is its saying ״with the daughters״ etc. And Scripture was precise to say <b>the people</b>, to exclude the righteous who are called by the name Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:09.445969354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}